{"version":1,"slug":"Others__Reasoning_-_VISUAL_REASONING_(15)_(20Q)","path":"Others/Reasoning - VISUAL REASONING (15) (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"Reasoning - VISUAL REASONING (15) (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Count the number of triangles in the given figure.</p><p><img width=479 height=274 id=\"Drawing 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13631/image003.gif\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=479 height=274 id=\"Drawing 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13631/image003.gif\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">20</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">23</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">21</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>There are 20 triangles in the given figure.</p><p>A, B, C, BC, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K, L, M, N, O, P, Q, PQ and R are the triangles.</p><p><img width=409 height=234 id=\"Drawing 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13631/image004.gif\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many rhombus are there in the given figure? </p><p><img width=198 height=200 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24612/image009.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=198 height=200 id=\"&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24612/image009.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">20</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>We know that,</p><p>All sides of a rhombus are equal and opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel.</p><p><img width=220 height=218 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24612/image010.jpg\"></p><p>Thus, the rhombuses are ABFD, BCGF, FGIJ, DFJK, ACIK, EFML, FHNM, MNOU, LMUS, EHOS, RQUV, QPTU, UTYX, VUXW and RPYW.</p><p>So, there are 15 rhombuses.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the number of straight lines in the following figure? </p><p><img width=240 height=153 id=\"Picture 12\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24685/image011.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=240 height=153 id=\"Picture 12\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24685/image011.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">13</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">11</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><img width=263 height=183 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24685/image012.jpg\"></p><p>Horizontal lines are CE, AL, MH, NQ.</p><p>Vertical lines are DN, FO, GP, EQ.</p><p>Slanting lines are AN, BC, DE, EH, QR.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many squares are there in the given figure? </p><p><img width=276 height=126 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25017/image011.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=276 height=126 id=\"&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25017/image011.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">34</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=302 height=158 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25017/image012.jpg\"></p><p>The squares are ABGF, BCHG, CDIH, DEJI, FGLK, GHML, HINM, IJON, PKSR, KLTS, LMUT, MNVU, NOWV, OQXW, ACMK, BDNL, CEOM, FHUS, GIVT, HJWU, ADVS, BEWT.</p><p>So, there are 22 squares.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Count the number of triangles in the given figure?</p><p><img width=395 height=323 id=\"Drawing 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p10520/image005.gif\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=\"395\" height=\"323\" id=\"Drawing 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p10520/image005.gif\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">34</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>There are 34 triangles in the given figure.</p><p>LKJ, HGF, LIM, MIN, NIO, OIF, LIN, MIO, NIF, LIO, MIF, LIF, UIT, ITS, UIS, LAB, DEF, LCM, MCN, NCO, OCF, LNC, MCO, CNF, LCO, LCF, CQR, CQP, PCR, CFM, CFI, CIO, CIM and CIL.</p><p><img width=506 height=418 id=\"Drawing 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p10520/image006.gif\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the number of triangles in the given figure?</p><p><img width=479 height=210 id=\"Drawing 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16131/image006.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"479\" height=\"210\" id=\"Drawing 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16131/image006.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">21</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>There are nineteen triangles in the given figure. </p><p>ALB, BLC, CLK, KLA, ABC, BCK, CKA, KAB, CKJ, JNM, JNO, JMO, JDC, JDE, JCE, EIF, IFH, HFG, AJC .</p><p><img width=455 height=222 id=\"Drawing 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16131/image007.gif\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the number of rectangles in the given figure? </p><p><img width=382 height=209 id=\"Drawing 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15815/image019.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"382\" height=\"209\" id=\"Drawing 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15815/image019.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">23</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>There are twenty-three rectangles in the given figure. </p><p>ABC3, CD23, DF12, ABD2, 3CF1, ABF1, DEGH, DHY0, EGY0, ZU4Y, XUTW, WTSV, XUSV, IJKR, RKLQ, QLMP, PMNO, IJLQ, RKMP, QLNO, IJMP, RKNO, IRNO. </p><p><img width=432 height=250 id=\"Drawing 19\" src=\"https://u1.