505\" height=\"208\" id=\"Drawing 20\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15650/image021.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">26</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">26</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>There are twenty-six rectangles in the given figure. </p><p>A01B, 01YZ, B12C, 12KY, A02C, 0ZK2, AZYB, BYKC, AZKC, D4FE, 3JI5, 5IHG, 3JHG, K910L, 9QP10, L10NM, 10PON, K9NM, 9QON, KQPL, LPOM, KQOM, TSR7, VU6W, W68X, VU8X. </p><p><img width=573 height=275 id=\"Drawing 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15650/image022.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many squares/rectangles are there in the given figure?</p><p><img width=425 height=259 id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6952/image023.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;/&#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=\"425\" height=\"259\" id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6952/image023.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">27</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">26</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">26</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">31</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">31</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><img width=457 height=273 id=\"Picture 23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6952/image024.jpg\"></p><p>Squares/rectangles in the given figure are  -  ABCD, EFGH, IJKL, MNOP, ERS3, ETU3, EGW3, 3FHW, RSTU, RNVT, RNXG, RSWG, IULZ, IV1L, TUWG, TVXG, TJYG, UVXW, UJYW, UV1Z, UVO2, WYKZ, WX1Z, WXO2, Z1O2, XYK1, JYXV, NSUV, NSWX, NSZ1, NS2O.</p><p><b>Total squares/rectangles = 31</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many squares are present in the given figure?</p><p><img width=173 height=173 id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6447/image013.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=\"173\" height=\"173\" id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6447/image013.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">17</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><img width=203 height=204 id=\"Picture 19\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6447/image014.jpg\"></p><p>Taking small squares (singles)</p><p>Number of squares in 1<sup>st</sup> row = 3</p><p>Number of squares in 2<sup>nd</sup> row = 3</p><p>Number of squares in 3<sup>rd</sup> row = 3</p><p>Number of squares in 4<sup>th</sup> row = 4</p><p>Number of squares formed by combination of 4 single squares = 4</p><p>Total squares in figure = 3+3+3+4+4 = <b>17</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many quadrilaterals are there in the given figure?</p><p><img width=216 height=186 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3438/image006.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=\"216\" height=\"186\" id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3438/image006.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><img width=249 height=222 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3438/image007.png\"></p><p>Quadrilaterals = FEMN, FAMN, BEMN, BAMN, HBNO, HGNO, CGNO, CBNO, IJPO, IDPO, CJPO, CDPO, DLMP, KLMP, KAMP, DAMP, LAEM, FBGN, HCIO, DKPJ, ABCD and MNOP = 22</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the total number of rectangles in the figure given below.</p><p><img width=248 height=245 id=\"Picture 12\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15830/image013.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"248\" height=\"245\" id=\"Picture 12\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15830/image013.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">13</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=279 height=264 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15830/image014.png\"></p><p>The rectangles are  -  ACDB, CEFD, EGHF, GIJH, AEFB, AGHB, AIJB, IJFE, IJDC, KFST, FMRS, KMRT, WVUT, RQPO, CGHD.</p><p>So, there are 15 rectangles. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the minimum number of straight lines to make the given figure.</p><p><img width=318 height=221 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5602/image001.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2351;&#2368; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p><p><img width=\"318\" height=\"221\" id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5602/image001.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>we get,</p><p><img width=376 height=268 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5602/image002.jpg\"></p><p>Minimum required straight lines are  -  AE, EW, WT, TA, HK, LG, MO, PS, CH, CK, FG, HU, IV and JS.</p><p><b>Total = 14</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many triangles are there in the given figure?</p><p><img width=205 height=126 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3322/image012.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; ?</p><p><img width=\"205\" height=\"126\" id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3322/image012.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">32</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><img width=299 height=205 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3322/image013.png\"></p><p>Triangles = MRV, NRW, NMA, VAZ, OSX, NSW, NOA, XAZ, OTX, OPA, TPU, AXY, PQU, QVM, AVY, APM, RNS, SOT, TPQ, RMQ, VZX, YZX, VYX, YZV, MNO, NOP, OPM and MNP.</p><p><b>Alternatively: -</b></p><p>Figure is symmetrical in 4 quadrants. So, let us count triangles in one of the quadrant and multiply it by 4.</p><p>In 1<sup>st</sup> quadrant: - MRV, NRW, NMA, VAZ there are 4 triangles.</p><p>So, in 4 quadrants there are 16 triangles.</p><p>Combining 2 quadrants we get 3 triangles viz. RNS, VZX and MNO.</p><p>So, total there are 12 triangles.</p><p>Total number of triangles = 16 + 12 = 28</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the number of triangles in the figure given below  - </p><p><img width=298 height=83 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12026/image001.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; -</p><p><img width=\"298\" height=\"83\" id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12026/image001.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">38</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">38</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">34</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Consider one square</p><p><img width=115 height=125 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12026/image002.jpg\"></p><p>AEB, AEC, ABC, BED, DEC, BCD, ABD and ACD are all possible triangles.</p><p>So, no. of triangles in one square = 8</p><p>So, by symmetry all 4 squares will have 8 triangles each</p><p>Thus, no. of triangles in all squares together considering one square at a time = 4*8 = 32</p><p>Now, consider all squares combined together </p><p><img width=313 height=131 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12026/image003.jpg\"></p><p>PQR, STU, RVW, ZST, QRV and TUY are all possible triangles</p><p>So, no. of triangles considering all squares combined together = 6</p><p>So, the total no. of triangles formed = 32 + 6 = 38</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Count the number of rectangles in the given figure?</p><p><img width=457 height=232 id=\"Drawing 29\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12128/image030.gif\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=\"457\" height=\"232\" id=\"Drawing 29\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12128/image030.gif\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>There are sixteen rectangles in the given figure. NMIH, RSAB, OLQP, LKTQ, KJUT, JFDU, OKTP, LJUQ, KFDT, OJUP, LFDQ, OFDP, JFEV, VEDU, VGCU and GEDC.</p><p><img width=502 height=266 id=\"Drawing 30\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12128/image031.gif\"></p> <br clear=all style='page-break-before:always'>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the total number of rectangles in the figure given below.</p><p><img width=267 height=235 id=\"Picture 41\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17197/image024.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"267\" height=\"235\" id=\"Picture 41\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17197/image024.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">17</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=317 height=278 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er230213t2nperr-001.png\"></p><p>The rectangles are: AOCB, YEHW, DFIV, JLSN, JLMK, LPRM, YPRW, EJKH, YJKW, YLMW, PJKR, PEHR, GHIV, KMSN, ELMH, DFGH, MQTX.</p><p>MQTX is considered as rectangle because all squares are rectangle.</p><p>So, there are 17 rectangles.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many triangles are present in the given figure?</p><p><img width=318 height=161 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5547/image009.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p><img width=\"318\" height=\"161\" id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5547/image009.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">28</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">26</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">26</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>There are <b>32</b> triangles in the given figure.</p><p><img width=365 height=196 id=\"Picture 12\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5547/image010.png\"></p><p>Triangles are  -  ABI, ACI, ACO, AGI, AOI, ACQ, AOQ, BCI, CIK, CIQ, COQ, DEI, DFI, DFL, DFN, DIL, DIH, DLN, EFI, FIJ, FIN, FLN, GIO, HIL, ILN, ILM, INM, IJN, IKQ, IPQ, IPO, IOQ.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the minimum number of straight lines to make the given figure.</p><p><img width=268 height=242 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5800/image007.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2351;&#2368; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p><p><img width=\"268\" height=\"242\" id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5800/image007.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">17</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=274 height=271 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5800/image008.jpg\"></p><p>Minimum required straight lines are  -  GC, CF, FH, HL, LG, IN, NJ, JK, KI, IJ, GH, LM, AC, AE, BD, BF.</p><p>Total = 16</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}